One objective for the next 90 days: sign your first four clients and build the daily rhythm that takes you to eight. Everything in this plan points at that number.

- **£7,800/month** Income at four clients (£1,950 x 4) - your 90-day target
- **4 clients** Needed to hit the 90-day income target at minimum fee
- **12 to 16 calls** Prospect calls needed to sign four clients (at 25 to 33% close rate)
- **300+ conversations** LinkedIn conversations needed to generate 12 to 16 booked calls

> **Why four, not six:** Your minimum fee is £1,950 and your capacity is eight. Four clients in 90 days is realistic and leaves room to price up before you fill the remaining seats. The plan targets four signed by week twelve, with a price review after client two or three.

### Week by week

- **Weeks 1 to 2:** Foundations locked. LinkedIn rewritten using the contractor's voice and the Harlow & Pike proof. Profit Coach page live and pointing to your calendar. BOSS Scorecard link active and tested. Practice email set up. Prospect list of 100 MDs and owners in HVAC, M&E and electrical contracting built from LinkedIn search and any existing contacts. Prospect call slots confirmed in your calendar: Mondays and Thursdays from 1pm. One outreach message drafted and ready. Nothing goes out until the profile is right - a warm message from a weak profile wastes the conversation.
- **Weeks 2 to 4:** First campaign live. Connection requests going out daily: 15 to 20 a day, targeted at MDs and owners in building services firms turning over £2m to £12m, within a sensible geography of Leeds and the wider Yorkshire and East Midlands patch. Replies handled same day, Monday to Thursday. Prospect list extended to 300 or more. First BOSS Scorecard shares going out to warm contacts and anyone who engages with content. Goal: 5 to 8 prospect calls booked before week four ends.
- **Weeks 4 to 8:** Calls running, first client signed. Two to three prospect calls a week on Mondays and Thursdays. Value sessions run for any qualified MD who wants to see the numbers rhythm in action before committing. First client signed and onboarded - Zander sits in on their job review and pricing discussion within the first two weeks of engagement. Content publishing four times a month on LinkedIn: short, specific posts rooted in real contracting problems. Goal: one to two clients signed by week eight.
- **Weeks 8 to 12:** Second campaign angle tested, price reviewed, referrals asked for. Second outreach angle tested alongside the first - try the retention cash problem if the margin bleed angle has been the opener, or target facilities management owners as a secondary segment. Price reviewed after client two or three: move from £1,950 to £2,450 for clients three and four as capacity fills. First referral ask made to any signed client who is getting early traction. Newsletter issue one drafted and sent to anyone who has engaged but not yet signed. Goal: four clients signed by week twelve.

